{"id": "whcarpathian", "name": "Primeval Beech Forests of the Carpathians", "short": "Carpathian Beech", "place": "Slovakia and Ukraine", "lat": 48.9, "lon": 22.5, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Slovakia", "countries": ["Slovakia", "Ukraine"], "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Ancient beech and fir forest where bears, wolves and lynx roam over deadwood.", "tip": {"id": "wolf", "title": "Remove the wolves", "text": "Wolves hunt red deer, roe deer and wild boar. Set Grey wolf to -100% and watch those herbivores and the forest plants they browse."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Ancient and Primeval Beech Forests of the Carpathians and Other Regions of Europe", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primeval_Beech_Forests_of_the_Carpathians_and_Other_Regions_of_Europe"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Poloniny National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poloniny_National_Park"}, {"title": "UNESCO World Heritage Centre: Ancient and Primeval Beech Forests", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1133/"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: White-backed woodpecker", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White-backed_woodpecker"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Eurasian lynx", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eurasian_lynx"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: European wildcat", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_wildcat"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Poloniny National Park", "icon": "whitebark", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Little light reaches the floor under a closed beech canopy, so the forest floor is shaded for much of the growing season."}, {"id": "climate", "sp": "cool, wet mountain climate", "xh": 0.35}, {"id": "deadwood", "sp": "standing and fallen deadwood", "xh"